# Repository layout note: the repo groups files by role (server/,
# data/, tools/, tests/). At runtime the server expects a FLAT
# directory: fssa_search_server.py + corpus files + embeddings +
# key files side by side. Deployment copies server/ and data/
# contents into that runtime directory.

# Secrets: never commit keys. Providers read *_key.txt files from
# the runtime server directory; keep yours local.
*_key.txt
*_key*.txt
*.key
.env
.env.*

# Generated embeddings: rebuild with the tools (see README).
embeddings.json
embeddings.jsonl
embeddings.npz
embeddings*.bak*

# Runtime state written by the server (spend ledger, guard
# counters, ask records): local to the runtime directory.
*_spend.json
*_usage.json
ask_records.jsonl
gap_log.jsonl

# Data backups and pipeline byproducts
*.bak
*.bak-*
corpus*.json.bak*
dedupe_log.jsonl
dedupe_skip.json

# QA / test working files (answer sets, harness output)
answers*.json
*_answers.json
answers/
situational/
test*.json
t_*.json

# Logs
*.log
*.err

# Build-session status/report docs (curated copies live in docs/
# as STATUS-v*.md; raw session files stay out)
STATUS.md
*_REPORT.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
